WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.053 --> 00:00:07.840
Speaker 1: Let's go next to where are we&nbsp;
going next? It's not clear. Let's go to J.T.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.080
from South Carolina. J.T., you're on the air.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.000
Hello, can you hear me? Yes, I can.
Speaker 2: Oh, nice to meet you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.760
David. Likewise. Long time. I'm a long&nbsp;
time watcher. Just want to know, have you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:28.800
recently been seeing the things circulating on&nbsp;
social media regarding trapped African exchange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.920
students in Ukraine and the treatment they've&nbsp;
been facing from the the authorities there?&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:40.240
Speaker 1: I have seen it and there there were&nbsp;
some incorrect reports about what was going on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:45.600
And some good reporting as well.&nbsp;
I have not read anything about it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.400
in the last three or four days. Is there something&nbsp;
in particular going on now that I've maybe missed?&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.760
Speaker 2: Well, no. It's just I'm calling from&nbsp;
South Carolina and I've been talking with a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.080
of people in my community and, you know,&nbsp;
the black community and how they how do you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.880
basically perceive this whole situation? And&nbsp;
I find that a lot of people in my community,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.120
and I'm not by no means speaking for everyone&nbsp;
in my community, just the people I've personally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:16.400
spoken with. I find out a lot of them have a hard&nbsp;
time garnering sympathy for the Ukrainians because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:22.240
that's all you see on social media nowadays,&nbsp;
with the Ukrainians being under constant threat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:28.000
from the Russians, how United States is sending&nbsp;
billions over there in aid and how the media is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.480
shining this light on this humanitarian crisis,&nbsp;
which I agree it's terrible, is going on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:40.880
Yet we all aren't shining the same light on people&nbsp;
suffering in South American countries or in in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:46.640
African countries that are facing similar threats.
Speaker 1: I mean, yeah, you know, that's that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:54.320
always an issue. And here's the thing, JT, you&nbsp;
know, we I've talked on my program endlessly about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:00.000
why, what determines what makes the news and what&nbsp;
doesn't. And there's all these different factors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.120
And one of those factors is certainly who is it&nbsp;
that is being oppressed? That's a factor. One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:11.040
hundred percent. That's a factor. What is that?&nbsp;
What is the profile of the people being oppressed?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:19.200
Other factors include Is it an oppression that&nbsp;
has a clear beginning, middle and end? And this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.600
is why sometimes long term suffering gets less&nbsp;
attention than an individual crisis that's like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:32.960
OK, Russia is about to invade. They've invaded.&nbsp;
There's now an invasion. And in principle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:38.960
at some point that invasion will stop. That also&nbsp;
is a reason why certain things get more attention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.880
and other things get less attention. So I think&nbsp;
those are all legitimate things to talk about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:50.560
It doesn't justify in any way what Russia is doing&nbsp;
and the value in repelling the invasion. So yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:54.800
I mean, I totally get what you're saying.
Speaker 2: Thank you. Thank you. And one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:02.000
final thing I want to point out is this is as&nbsp;
if the Republicans have had a whole 180 about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.520
the immigration status of the Ukraine. They want&nbsp;
to bring a lot of Ukrainians over here. Yet we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:15.200
just expelled over 4000 Haitians just last year.
Speaker 1: I know here, I know the if you want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:21.920
find hypocrisy and fickleness, look at American&nbsp;
immigration policy. That is without a doubt that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.960
you can always count on that.
Speaker 2: Oh, well, thank you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.200
my friend for taking my question. I'm finally glad&nbsp;
I finally go on the show. I appreciate it so much.&nbsp;

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.640
Speaker 1: JT, it's been a pleasure.&nbsp;
Thank you. Thank you. All right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:38.480
there's JT from South Carolina making&nbsp;
a number of different important points.

